## Checkpoint (continue / retomar)

Keep `.claude/state/checkpoint.json` live (cursor-kit schema). Hooks fill `files` and `updated_at`; you own the rest.

- When a multi-step task ends, or you stop mid-task, write `task`, `status` (`in_progress`, `blocked` or `done`),
  `pending`, `blockers` and `next_action`. Keep the other keys.
- On `continue` or `retomar`, read it first and resume from `next_action`. If `task` is empty, ask what to resume.
- Short labels and file paths only: no secrets, no personal or patient data, no message, draft or report text.
